A||||4||stsmithgt||My smog got catagorized||||13||
Z||000000||stsmithgt||10-19-2000||05:43 PM||||Get this.  Since my smog check failed.  They said they would set the timing and check it again. OK  Instead of waiting around, I went to work.  I call them 4 and a half hours later thinking it was done. NOT!  Now that it failed the initial test, they consider it a "smog repair". Which I didn't have an appointment for.  Mine was only for the "Check". SOOooo they haven't touched my car all day due to the other cars that have appointments before mine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  If I knew that's how it worked, I would have taken it down the street to get it done.  I was hoping to get it done TODAY. geezz.<BR>More venting.  I hope they like a black striped driveway if it's not done by the time I get there after work.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <P>Is this a normal practice for an auto center? I must be nieve.........sigh....<P><p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 10-19-2000).]||||reg||13
Z||000001||tgowens||10-20-2000||03:10 AM||||wellllllllllll, hmmmmmmmm, I think that it's a little bit of hooey myself!! Normally, timing won't fail a smog check but a bad O2 sensor or cat will (that's catalytic convertor to you frog guys - us cat lovers KNOW what it means!) (he says with a smug grin as he finishes off another of those little green bottles)-- we didn't replace the O2 sensor when you were here you know. <P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                          <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT<p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 10-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||stsmithgt||10-20-2000||02:30 PM||||I don't recall that being one of the sensors I've had replaced.  My "cat" is not a year old.  I'll have to check my records on that O2 sensor back on my lilly pad to see if I've had it replaced. It's a wonder how that cat and that dogbone get along so well....(I know, it's a cheesy joke)||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||10-20-2000||02:36 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> cute joke..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>  unfortunatly many shops are like that.. they've got your car what are you gunna do about it? take it somwhere else? oh darn i's tore apart sorry.. yeah.. happend to me a few times too... <P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||stsmithgt||10-20-2000||03:04 PM||||Oh well, before I bought this car, I usually did the work myself.(had a 66 chevy P-UP)<BR>I think my timing might be getting advanced a little from stock (all by itself, can you believe that).  It didn't ping at 20 BTDC, but my Idle was a hair rough.  My foot liked the performance improvement with the timing more advanced.  I don't think the gremlins the work on my car in the middle of the night will put it back to 20 BTDC, but maybe a few more degrees advanced.  I wouldn't do it myself.  That's not smog legal. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||12
